          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#general_idea General idea
          %p
            What are called a
            %strong homotopy quantum field theories
            (HQFTs) are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+quantum+field+theories"} topological quantum field theories
            (TQFT) defined on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordisms"} cobordisms
            that are equipped with the extra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            into a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            Hence if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Bord
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bord_n(B)
            denotes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+cobordisms"} category of cobordisms
            suitably equipped with maps into
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+functor"} monoidal functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Bord
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo ⊗
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Z \;\colon\; Bord_n(B)^{\coprod} \longrightarrow Vect^{\otimes}
                  \\,.
          %h3#history History
          %p
            HQFTs were first defined (under a different name) by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"} Graeme Segal
            as early as 1988 in (
            %a{:href => "#Segal88"}> Segal 88
            ).
          %p
            Starting from 1991, several papers by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"} Dan Freed
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FreedQuinn1991"} FreedQuinn1991
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+field+theory"} functorial field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg%E2%80%93MacLane+space"} Eilenberg–MacLane space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(G,1)
            for a finite group
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#FreedQuinn1991"} FreedQuinn1991
          %p
            From 1999, HQFTs were studied systematically by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Turaev"} Vladimir Turaev
            (
            %a{:href => "#Turaev99"}> Turaev 99
            ) for 2-dimensional
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordisms"} cobordisms
            and extended to 3-dimensional ones in (
            %a{:href => "#Turaev00"}> Turaev 00
            ). Turaev also introduced the term “homotopy quantum field theory”.
          %p
            At about the same time, (
            %a{:href => "#BrightwellTurner00"}> Brightwell-Turner 00
            ) looked at what they called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            surface category and its
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            already given by
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TQFT"} TQFT
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-models"} sigma-models
          %p
            In the proof of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
            in (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/On+the+Classification+of+Topological+Field+Theories"}> Lurie 09
            ) the concept of HQFTs was refined to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+TQFT"} extended TQFT
            by considering an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category+of+cobordisms"} (∞,n)-category of cobordisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Bord
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bord_n(X)
            with maps to a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
            essentially says (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "cobordism+hypothesis#StatementForCobordismsInAManifold"} For framed cobordisms in a topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Bord
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bord_n(X)^\coprod
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free construction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category+with+duals"} (∞,n)-category with duals
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} fundamental ∞-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X)
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            An HQFT is going to be defined as assigning data to
            = succeed "-cobordisms." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#BCobordism"} B-cobordisms
          %p and then define
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#HQFTs"} HQFTs
          %p themselves in terms of these.
          %h3#BCobordism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            \-Cobordisms
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"} pointed topological space
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                \-manifold
              is a pair
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, g)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a closed oriented
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              (with a choice of base point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi m
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_i
              in each connected component
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i
              of
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : X \to B
              = succeed "," do
                %strong characteristic map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi m
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(m_i) = \ast
              for each base point
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_i
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                \-isomorphism
              between
              = succeed "-manifolds," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : ( X, g) \to ( Y, h)
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : X \to Y
              of the manifolds, preserving the orientation, taking base points into base points and such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\phi = g
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              If as is often the case, the manifolds under consideration will be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              and then ‘
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"}> isomorphism
              ’ is interpreted as ‘
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"}> diffeomorphism
              ’, but equally well we can position the theory in the category of PL-manifolds or triangulable topological manifolds with the obvious changes. In fact for some of the time it is convenient to develop constructions for simplicial complexes rather than manifolds, as it is triangulations that provide the basis for the combinatorial descriptions of the structures that we will be using.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Denote by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Man
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Man}(n,B)
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              = succeed "-dimensional" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-manifolds" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              = succeed "-isomorphisms." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
              = succeed "-manifolds" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⨿
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⨿
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo ⨿
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ( X, g) \amalg ( Y, h) := ( X\amalg Y, g\amalg h),
            %p
              with the obvious characteristic map,
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ⨿
                      %mi h
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⨿
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\amalg h : X \amalg Y \to B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Man
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Man}(n,B)
              becomes a symmetric monoidal category with the unit being given by the empty
              = succeed "-manifold," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset
              = succeed "-manifold" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            These
            = succeed "-manifolds" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordisms"} cobordisms
            for this setting.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A
              = succeed "," do
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  \-cobordism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi W
                      %mo ,
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (W,F)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_0,g)
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_1,h)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W : X_0 \to X_1
              endowed with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+class"} homotopy class
              relative to the boundary of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi W
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : W \to B
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F|_{X_0} =  g \,, \;\;\;\;  F|_{X_1} = h
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Generally, unless necessary in this entry, we will not make a notational distinction between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+class"} homotopy class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              and any of its representatives.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              A
              = succeed "," do
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  \-isomorphism of
                  = succeed "-cobordisms" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi W
                      %mo ,
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi W
                        %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                          %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi F
                        %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                          %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi : (W,F) \to (W^\prime, F^\prime)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo :
                    %mi W
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                        %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi : W \to W^\prime
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mo +
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                        %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mo −
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mo −
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                        %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi (\partial_+W) = \partial_+W^\prime, \quad \psi (\partial_-W) = \partial_-W^\prime,
            %p
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi F
                        %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                          %mo ′
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo =
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^\prime \psi = F
          %p
            We can glue
            = succeed "-cobordisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed "-isomorphism" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi HCobord
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{HCobord}(n,B)
            of
            = succeed "-cobordisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            The detailed structure of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordisms"} cobordisms
            and the resulting category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi HCobord
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{HCobord}(n,B)
            is given in (
            %a{:href => "#Rodrigues03"}> Rodrigues 03, appendix
            ), at least in the important case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth
            = succeed "-manifolds." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            with strict
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+objects"} dual objects
          %h3#HQFTs Homotopy Quantum Field Theories
          %p The general absract definition of an HQFT is now the following.
          %p
            Fix an integer
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 0
            and a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            can be replaced by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            merely by replacing finite dimensional vector spaces by projective
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            of finite type, but we will not do this here.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong homotopy quantum field theory
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+functor"} symmetric monoidal functor
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi HCobord
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{HCobord}(n,B)
              to the category,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %p This definiting unwinds to the following structure in components
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              A
              = succeed "," do
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n + 1)
                  \-dimensional homotopy quantum field theory
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              assigns
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  to any
                  = succeed "-dimensional" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  = succeed "-manifold," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi τ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau{(X,g)}
              %li
                %p
                  to any
                  = succeed "-isomorphism," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo :
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo →
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %mo ,
                          %mi h
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : (X, g) \to ( Y, h)
                  = succeed "-dimensional" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  = succeed "-manifolds," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  = succeed "-linear" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi τ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo :
                          %mi τ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo →
                          %mi τ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ,
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau(\phi)  : \tau{(X, g)} \to \tau{( Y, h)}
            %p and
            %ul
              %li
                to any
                = succeed "-cobordism," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi W
                        %mo ,
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (W,F) : (X_0,g_0) \to (X_1,g_1)
                = succeed "-linear" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi τ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mi τ
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi τ
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau(W) : \tau{(X_0,g_0)} \to \tau{(X_1,g_1)}
            %p These assignments are to satisfy the following axioms:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi τ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
                  is functorial in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi Man
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo ,
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Man}(n,B)
                  = succeed "-isomorphisms," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi h
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi: (X, g) \to ( Y, h)
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo :
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %mo ,
                          %mi h
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo →
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi P
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : ( Y, h) \to (P,j)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi τ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi τ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi τ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau(\phi\psi) = \tau(\phi)\tau(\psi),
                  and if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_{(X,g)}
                  is the identity
                  = succeed "-isomorphism" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi τ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mi τ
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo ,
